# Content Plan: Streamlit Dashboard "Bait" Post

## 1. Goal & Target Audience

**Primary Goal:** Drive developers to the Sentimatix portal to register for a Free-Tier API Key.
**Secondary Goal:** Get stars on the open-source Streamlit GitHub repository (which acts as long-term SEO).
**Target Audience:** Python developers, retail quantitative traders, data scientists interested in the Indian stock market.

---

## 2. Title Options

Pick one based on your tone:

| Angle | Title |
|---|---|
| Tutorial | *How I built a Real-Time NSE Stock Sentiment Dashboard in 50 Lines of Python* |
| Contrarian | *Bloomberg Terminals are expensive. I built a free alternative for Indian Retail Traders.* |
| Technical | *Using FinBERT and Streamlit to analyze live NSE/BSE Sentiment* |
| Curiosity | *What if your Python script could read market sentiment before you trade?* |

---

## 3. Article Outline & Draft Structure

### Section 1 — The Hook (First 150 words are critical)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is the most important section. If the reader doesn't feel the pain, they won't read further.

**Draft Narrative:**
- **The Problem:** Institutional traders have access to Bloomberg, Refinitiv, and proprietary NLP pipelines. Retail traders in India are flying blind — they rely on headlines and Twitter noise to gauge market sentiment.
- **The Payoff:** Open with your dashboard screenshot/GIF. Show something visually compelling first. Let the reader see the end result before they read a single line of code.
- *Example opening line:* "I wanted to know how the market *feels* about Reliance before the open. Not what analysts say — what the actual news flow says, right now. So I built this."

---

### Section 2 — The Architecture (Keep it short)

Explain the stack in 2–3 sentences:
- **UI Layer:** Streamlit (Python, zero frontend needed)
- **Data/Intelligence Layer:** Sentimatix API (FinBERT-powered NLP on Indian financial news)
- **Hosting:** Streamlit Community Cloud (free)

Position the Sentimatix API as the component that saves them *months* of building their own scraper + NLP pipeline.

---

### Section 3 — The Core Code (The Value Transfer)

> [!TIP]
> Keep each code block under 20 lines. Long code blocks lose readers. Show one concept per block.

**Block 1 — Fetching sentiment data:**
```python
import requests

url = "https://api.sentimatix.com/api/v1/sentiment/symbol/RELIANCE.NS"
headers = {"X-API-Key": "YOUR_FREE_KEY"}

response = requests.get(url, headers=headers).json()
print(response['sentiment_score'])  # e.g. 0.72 (Bullish)
```

**Block 2 — Displaying in Streamlit:**
```python
import streamlit as st

st.metric(
    label="Reliance — Sentiment Score",
    value=f"{response['sentiment_score']:.2f}",
    delta="Bullish" if response['sentiment_score'] > 0.5 else "Bearish"
)

# Show top news articles driving the sentiment
for article in response['articles'][:3]:
    st.write(f"📰 {article['title']}")
```

Narrate each block — don't just dump code. Explain *why* each line matters.

---

### Section 4 — The Open Source Handoff (The Bait)

This is where you hand them the full repo:
- Link to the GitHub repository
- Show a screenshot of the repo's README
- *Draft text:* "I've open-sourced the entire dashboard. Clone it, tweak the visuals, plug in your own watchlist, or wire it up to a Telegram bot for alerts. The only thing you need is a free Sentimatix API key to fetch the live data."

---

### Section 5 — The CTA (The Conversion)

This must be the last thing they read. Be direct.

**Draft CTA block:**
> Ready to build your own? The Sentimatix API has a **Free Tier** with 100 calls/day — enough to build, backtest, and explore.
>
> 👉 **[Get your free API key → sentimatix-production.up.railway.app/portal](https://sentimatix-production.up.railway.app/portal)**
>
> If you found this useful, drop a ⭐ on the [GitHub repo](#) — it genuinely helps.

---

## 4. Technical SEO & Medium-Specific Tips

- **Tags to use on Medium:** `Python`, `Stock Market`, `Fintech`, `Machine Learning`, `Data Science`
- **Publication to submit to:** [Towards Data Science](https://towardsdatascience.com/) or [Better Programming](https://betterprogramming.pub/) (both are major Medium publications with large developer audiences — submission is free)
- **Reading time target:** Aim for 5–7 minutes (≈ 1,200–1,600 words). Long enough to be credible, short enough to finish.
- **First image:** The GIF/screenshot must be the *very first* thing after the title. Medium's algorithm uses it as the post thumbnail.

---

## 5. Cross-Platform Distribution Checklist

Publishing on Medium is only 20% of the work. Distribution is 80%.

- [ ] **Medium / Towards Data Science:** Publish the core article.
- [ ] **Dev.to & Hashnode:** Republish the same article word-for-word. These platforms have zero paywall and a higher dev density than Medium.
- [ ] **Reddit** (`r/Python`, `r/developersIndia`, `r/algotrading`, `r/SideProject`): Copy-paste the *full tutorial text* into a Reddit text post (do NOT just drop a link — you will be flagged as spam). Mention the API key at the very bottom only.
- [ ] **Hacker News ("Show HN"):** Submit the **GitHub repo link** (not the Medium post) with the title: `Show HN: Open-source Streamlit dashboard for real-time NSE/BSE sentiment analysis`.
- [ ] **LinkedIn:** Post the dashboard GIF with a 3-line hook. Put the Medium article link in the **first comment** (LinkedIn's algorithm suppresses posts with external links in the body).
- [ ] **X / Twitter:** Same strategy as LinkedIn. Post the GIF, engage for 1 hour, then drop the link in a reply thread.

---

## 6. Timing Recommendation

Post between **Tuesday–Thursday, 9–11 AM IST**. This catches Indian developers at the start of their workday and maximizes early engagement, which is critical for Medium's internal distribution algorithm.
